WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.740
So what would they do for a cold?

2
00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:08.760
Well, Grandma, she had something that she'd go out to get out there and come back, make you a tea.

3
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:13.320
Drink that and in a few days you was all right.

4
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:18.080
I remember my brother, he had what . . . malaria fever.

5
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.780
They called it malaria fever, I think they called it.

6
00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.660
Anyway, he had that one year.

7
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.460
He was serious sick with that fever, you know, high fever.

8
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.780
They had what these . . . called them bitter weeds.

9
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.380
Whole big weed with those yellow flowers on them.

10
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.980
They come up about so high.

11
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.980
They made us go pull a lot of them.

12
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.980
They had a big wash pot on the outside.

13
00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:47.060
A big old pot they put water in it and throwed wood around it, Got it hot.

14
00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:53.780
Got them bitter weeds and put them in that tubs back then.

15
00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:57.080
They didn't have the tub like they got in the bathroom then.

16
00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.100
They had this wash tub.

17
00:00:59.100 --> 00:00:59.980
The number three tub?

18
00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:00.580
Yeah.

19
00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:01.520
Number three tub.

20
00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:06.500
They put them bitter weeds in there and poured that hot water in there on that.

21
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:16.500
They put a . . . Set a chair in there and set him in that chair and covered him up with a blanket and sweated him out.

22
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.140
In a few days he was all right.

23
00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.280
What about for cuts or bruises or anything like that?

24
00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:22.660
Yeah.

25
00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:28.730
They would put some turpentine on it.

26
00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:32.220
We called it coal oil back then, kerosene.

27
00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.740
They poured kerosene on it?

28
00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:38.236
Yeah, pour kerosene on it and turpentine.

29
00:01:38.236 --> 00:01:49.160
I believe they’d put that on there and then they’d go around the house and get some spider webs, you know, spider webs.

30
00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.500
Put that on there and wrap it up.

31
00:01:51.500 --> 00:02:08.380
I . . . spot on my foot there where I was out to the cow pen when I was smaller and had . . . see the [tin?] around the side there and I climbed up on the . . . and slid down that.

32
00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:11.760
Cut my foot all open under there.

33
00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.960
Got around the house got that put on it, wrapped it up.

34
00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:22.540
I was walking on my heel for a few days, but after that it got all right.

35
00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:28.140
We didn't go to no doctor for nothing like that, just a cut like that.

36
00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:34.740
Now, I don't remember breaking no bones or nothing so . . . They didn't have no money to waste.

37
00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:43.462
You cut your foot you didn't have no money to go to the doctor with that. [laughs]

38
00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:43.721
You just tough it out.

39
00:02:43.721 --> 00:02:43.921
Yeah.

40
00:02:43.773 --> 00:02:44.780
It'll be alright in a few days.

41
00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:46.200
Stuck a nail.

42
00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.060
I stuck a nail in my foot.

43
00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:54.120
They put a piece of fat meat on that.

44
00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:54.680
Bacon.

45
00:02:54.680 --> 00:03:02.640
Fat meat and bacon, slap piece . . . Cut a piece out, put it on there and wrap it up, for a nail stick.

46
00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:06.888
Pour some turpentine or something like that on it.

47
00:03:06.888 --> 00:03:08.580
Go on.

48
00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.040
What was the turpentine for?

49
00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.600
That would take some of the soreness out of it and make it heal, too.

50
00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:18.700
Kerosene be the same thing.

51
00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:21.800
Take some of the soreness out of it, and it heal up.
